rm T$ |\n\nThen, we add a column for $X \\lor \\neg Y{:}$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\, \\neg Y \\,$ | $\\, X \\lor \\neg Y \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ |\n\nFinally, we add a column for $X \\land (X \\lor \\neg Y){:}$\n\n| $\\,X\\,$ | $\\,Y\\,$ | $\\, \\neg Y \\,$ | $\\, X \\lor \\neg Y \\,$ | $\\, X \\land (X \\lor \\neg Y) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186157017 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\,$ | $\\,\\neg (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n\nUse your results to determine whether $\\neg A \\land \\neg B$ is logically equivalent to $\\neg (A \\lor B).$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186157017 1071 "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\,$ | $\\,\\neg (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\phantom{F}}$ |\n\nUse your results to determine whether $\\neg A \\land \\neg B$ is logically equivalent to $\\neg (A \\lor B)$." 13194139533452 17592186045585 false] [17592186157017 1074 "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm T$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm F$, we have\n$¬A∧¬B \\mid ≡¬T∧¬F; ≡F∧T; ≡F$\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm F$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm T$, we have\n$¬(A∨B) \\mid ≡¬(F∨T); ≡¬T; ≡F$\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm F$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm F$, we have\n$¬(A∨B) \\mid ≡¬(F∨F); ≡¬F; ≡T$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\,$ | $\\,\\neg (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n\nTo determine whether\n\n$$\n\\neg A \\land \\neg B\n$$\n\nis logically equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\lor B)\n$$\n\nwe need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\textrm{F},\\textrm{F},\\textrm{F},\\textrm{T})$. Therefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\neg A \\land \\neg B\n$$\n\nis logically equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\neg (A \\lor B)\n$$\n\nthat is,\n\n$$\n\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\equiv} \\neg (A \\lor B)\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 false] [17592186157017 1074 "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm T$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm F,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬A∧¬B & ≡¬\\text{T}∧¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∧\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm F$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∨B) & ≡¬(\\text{F}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A \\equiv \\textrm F$ and $B \\equiv \\textrm F,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(A∨B) & ≡¬(\\text{F}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\,$ | $\\,\\neg (A \\lor B) \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ | $\\textrm F$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm F}$ |\n| $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm F$ | $\\textrm T$ | $\\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\textrm T}$ |\n\n \n\nTo determine whether $\\neg A \\land \\neg B$ is logically equivalent to $\\neg (A \\lor B),$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nLooking at the last two columns, we see that they are the same $(\\textrm{F},\\textrm{F},\\textrm{F},\\textrm{T}).$ Therefore, we conclude that $\\neg A \\land \\neg B$ is logically equivalent to $\\neg (A \\lor B),$ that is,\n\n$$\n\\neg A \\land \\neg B \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\equiv} \\neg (A \\lor B).\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186157018 1071 "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\n- $B \\land \\neg A$\n\n- $\\neg (A \\lor \\neg B)$\n\n- $\\neg (\\neg A \\lor B)$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186157018 1071 "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n\n1. $B \\land \\neg A$\n2. $\\neg (A \\lor \\neg 