f parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=2x?$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375679 1072 #uuid "abc2c374-a8d6-547c-a2fc-d8046e852f7f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375679 1074 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =2x \\\\ 4p & =2 \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y=2(\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y=t.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375681 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375682 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375683 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375684 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375685 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375683 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375680 1080 #uuid "7e971284-4599-5c77-9487-0d40be9f2ca4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375681 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375681 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375681 1084 #uuid "56929ae7-8267-56bb-bd8e-fbce73d8d772" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375682 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=2t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375682 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375682 1084 #uuid "b3ca7528-dc7b-50ef-b046-eab1a289ab1f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375683 1081 "x=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375683 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375683 1084 #uuid "c9493ea6-d33f-5c4f-84b2-c812441df81d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375684 1081 "x=2{t}^{2},\\,\\,y=4t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375684 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375684 1084 #uuid "101ce319-ab20-5d8c-8a08-c008a02ebd5e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375685 1081 "x={t}^{2},\\,\\,y=t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375685 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375685 1084 #uuid "fdcd8930-a6c4-5099-bcb2-dd8030e79cd1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375687 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1069 "q-106444" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1071 "Find the Cartesian equation of the parabola defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=18{t}^{2},\\,y=3t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1072 #uuid "600cd2ef-b6ac-5285-91f8-e79fc7695ecb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375686 1074 "First, let's make $t$ the subject of the parametric equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{x}{18},\\,t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring both sides of the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now eliminate the parameter $t$ by substituting the above into the equation ${t}^{2}=\\frac{x}{18}$ and rearranging to find the Cartesian equation of the parabola, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =\\frac{x}{18} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian equation of the parabola is ${y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375688 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375689 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375690 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375691 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375692 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375688 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375687 1080 #uuid "38969e85-7a76-5148-8c19-00dbf529e8c0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375688 1081 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375688 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375688 1084 #uuid "534d4541-d091-5c0c-974b-38f2f17797ff" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375689 1081 "{y}^{2}=2x" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375689 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375689 1084 #uuid "80d336e9-4493-58c8-ab35-5e2b0addd2a2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375690 1081 "{y}^{2}=6x" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375690 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375690 1084 #uuid "109e5f0b-1776-5d6c-ac4b-23a89fc88226" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375691 1081 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{6}x" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375691 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375691 1084 #uuid "555c9c01-f5dc-5459-87fd-75b658510a61" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375692 1081 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}x" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375692 1084 #uuid "8db88381-448e-5780-a08c-ec04fd6e738e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375694 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1069 "q-106672" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- **If** $1=1,$ **then** $2\\le 3.$\n- **If** $1>1,$ **then** $2=3.$\n- **If** $1\\le 1,$ **then** $2>3.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1072 #uuid "fe214e05-59ed-5ab5-8013-1b438614f754" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375693 1074 "An implication $A⇒B$ is true *unless* $A$ is true and $B$ is false. In other words, the implication is true unless the \"promise\" is broken.\n\n- Statement I is true.  The antecedent $1=1$ is true, and the consequent $2\\le 3$ is true. So the promise is kept, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement II is true. The antecedent $1>1$ is false, so the promise does not apply. Regardless of the consequent, the promise is *not* broken, and the statement is true.\n\n- Statement III is false. The antecedent $1\\le 1$ is true, and the consequent $2>3$ is false. So the promise is broken, and the statement is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375695 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375696 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375697 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375698 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375699 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375698 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375694 1080 #uuid "30107b35-d8ac-5543-aee1-f602236b1d66" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375695 1081 "I only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375695 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375695 1084 #uuid "f5923f4a-60ff-5118-a342-cd5fc869a636" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375696 1081 "III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375696 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375696 1084 #uuid "01c8adfc-18ba-58bd-8059-f1bba7f9fbbf" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375697 1081 "None" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375697 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375697 1084 #uuid "e230e8a8-6848-5754-aea3-c71ed9b2c5e8" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375698 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375698 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375698 1084 #uuid "12cdf2df-dc2c-561f-becf-8f3aa8daff29" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375699 1081 "II only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375699 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375699 1084 #uuid "cad42179-1b70-55d7-9ca6-55b426f2d7f0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375700 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375701 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375700 1069 "q-106759" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375700 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375700 1071 "Given that\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -9 & -16\\end{aligned}]$ \nhas the LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}\\cdot {u}_{12}=$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375700 1072 #uuid "0fd7a569-3ee6-5b8c-8dc0-