0ba00-7ddf-5c52-9f44-145186ff8ecb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375738 1081 "4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375738 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375738 1084 #uuid "bad4ebeb-0126-5838-bc1c-c8eb244917c3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375739 1081 "5" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375739 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375739 1084 #uuid "d0664dbc-1e07-5e41-87a0-013479bfb5b6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375741 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1069 "q-109926" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1071 "Suppose that a matrix $D$ has characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}(\\lambda -3)^{8}(\\lambda +12)^{6},$ the rank of $(D-3I)^{4}$ equals $9,$ and the rank of $(D-3I)^{5}$ equals $8.$ If a basis of ${R}^{16}$ consists of linearly independent generalized eigenvectors of $D$, how many of these are generalized eigenvectors of rank $5$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3?$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1072 #uuid "c8f2e0c6-0647-57c4-a136-1d5064af2223" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375740 1074 "For the given matrix $D$ with eigenvalue $\\lambda =3,$ a generalized eigenvector of rank $5$ is a vector $v$ such that \n\n$$\n(D-3I)^{5}v=0\\,\\text{and}\\,(D-3I)^{4}v\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ must be a $16\\times 16$ matrix.\n\n- Since the rank of $(D-3I)^{4}$ equals $9,$ then by the rank-nullity theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D-3I)^{4}=16-9=7.\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions to $(D-3I)^{4}v=0$ form a subspace $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{4}$ of dimension $7$ in ${R}^{16}.$\n\n- Since the rank of $(D-3I)^{5}$ equals $8,$  then by the rank-nullity theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D-3I)^{5}=16-8=8.\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions to $(D-3I)^{5}v=0$ form a subspace $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{5}$ of dimension $8$ in ${R}^{16}.$\n\nSince $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{4}$ is a subspace of dimension $7$ in $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{5}$, which is a subspace of dimension $8,$ our basis can contain only $1$ vector that lies in $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{5}$ but does not lie in $\\text{Null}(D-3I)^{4}.$\n\nTherefore, there will be \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D-3I)^{5}-\\text{nullity}(D-3I)^{4}=8-7=1\n$$\n\n generalized eigenvector of rank $5$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375742 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375743 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375744 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375745 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375746 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375743 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375741 1080 #uuid "590ba047-135b-5692-b98d-d34851d9e5a3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375742 1081 "3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375742 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375742 1084 #uuid "d77cf98f-dc2d-597e-a58a-381d47b24fec" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375743 1081 "1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375743 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375743 1084 #uuid "83ff8887-2c73-56fe-b953-d516e5ec148d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375744 1081 "4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375744 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375744 1084 #uuid "119ebc3c-0a43-527e