375796 1068 #edb/ref 17592186375797 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375796 1069 "q-117711" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375796 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375796 1071 "![](images/6f/6f1cd478f596aa904dc9b1e254c2eb2873b264935cc11b2c3480fc3560d08d55.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x),$ shown above, consists of three line segments. Find the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375796 1072 #uuid "b27fcc87-93b0-5936-a3e8-30ac2641ea7f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375796 1074 "We divide the interval of integration into $4$ regions: the line segment for $x\\in [-4,-3),$ the line segment for $x\\in [-3,-2],$ the line segment for $x\\in [-2,1],$ and the line segment for $x\\in (1,4].$ Therefore, we can write the required integral as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{-3}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}+{{{\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{3}}+{{{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{4}}\n$$\n\n- The $1$st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-4,-3).$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-4}^{-3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-1.5.\n$$\n\n- The $2$nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-3,-2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(bh) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-2,1].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4+1)(3) \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,4].$ The corresponding region is a rectangle, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =bh \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{4}=-6.\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}-{A}_{4} \\\\  & =-1.5+1.5+7.5-6 \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375798 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375799 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375800 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375801 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375802 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375801 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375797 1080 #uuid "90b0d283-2886-5977-9bb3-c8d7120e94e6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375798 1081 "2.5" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375798 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375798 1084 #uuid "5cd9df66-421a-5f07-bf23-4a6ad42b8ce6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375799 1081 "2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375799 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375799 1084 #uuid "b1023bbb-194a-5d8e-aba1-bcbc3ff2acfb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 tru