 tangent to the given curve as a function of the arc length $s.$ Since we are given the curve $r(s)$ parametrized by the arc length $s$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(s)=‖{T}^{′}(s)‖=‖{r}^{″}(s)‖\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(s)$ and ${r}^{″}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡s,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s⟩ \\\\ {r}^{″}(s) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(0),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(s) & =‖{r}^{″}(s)‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡s)}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡s)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡s+{cos}^{2}⁡s} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375938 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375939 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375940 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375941 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375942 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1079 #edb/ref 17592186375941 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375937 1080 #uuid "bb321e95-8036-5305-85cc-8daac472f444" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375938 1081 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375938 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375938 1084 #uuid "e3a2b495-5ade-5c9a-9d43-e728c9e4e7