re orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]+1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375966 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375967 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375968 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375969 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1075 #edb/ref 17592186375970 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186375965 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 