3452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376138 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1069 "q-163675" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1071 "A particle $P$ of mass $4\\,kg$ moves along the $x$-axis under the action of a resultant force. The displacement of the particle is given by $(2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2})\\,m,$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in seconds. Calculate the work done by the force between the times $t=0\\,s$ and $t=1\\,s.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1072 #uuid "2946ea8d-fc5d-5e1c-a7ad-b8ebee7d21a3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376137 1074 "The work-energy principle states that the work done by a resultant force on a particle equals the change in the particle's kinetic energy. That is,\n\n$$\nW=Δ\\,\\text{KE}\n$$\n\nwhere the change in kinetic energy of a particle is given by\n\n$$\nΔ\\,\\text{KE}=\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{1}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}m{v}_{0}^{2}\n$$\n\nand $m$ is the particle's mass, ${v}_{0}$ is its initial velocity, and ${v}_{1}$ is its final velocity.\n\nThe displacement of the particle is given by $x(t)=2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2},$ where $t$ is time in seconds.\nWe find the velocity $v(t)$ of the particle by differentiating the displacement with respect to time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =6{t}^{2}+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the particle's initial velocity, at $t=0$, is\n\n$$\n{v}_{0}=v(0)=6(0)^{2}+2(0)=0\\,m/s,\n$$\n\nand final velocity, at $t=1$, is\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=v(1)=6(1)^{2}+2(1)=8\\,m/s.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the work-energy principle, the work done by the force between these times is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W & =Δ\\,\\text{KE} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot {8}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot {0}^{2} \\\\  & =128-0 \\\\  & =128\\,J.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376139 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376140 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376141 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376142 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376143 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1079 #edb/ref 17592186376143 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376138 1080 #uuid "abf10214-129c-5273-9a15-d862fef6c64e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376139 1081 "132\\,J" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376139 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376139 1084 #uuid "cc1a8e88-caed-5cb8-b087-8aa21552c9bb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376140 1081 "64\\,J" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376140 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376140 1084 #uuid "98965c6f-696f-5b4b-a818-d4ee3eed08ce" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376141 1081 "78\\,J" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376141 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376141 1084 #uuid "f124a2ef-b71c-5f40-b426-4271c9bbfd72" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376142 1081 "96\\,J" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376142 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376142 1084 #uuid "7ccabb96-6694-5d14-8af3-a3f18d64a23e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376143 1081 "128\\,J" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376143 1084 #uuid "83ee8dfa-ac8a-5f7b-b0f7-d8c07168808d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376145 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1069 "q-165431" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1071 "![](images/2f/2fcd9d22de989857e3c19379c44e9bd49a410fc0beeb40c34ea1e0040a8c0b72.png)\n\nWhat is the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above?" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1072 #uuid "84fa56a0-128a-5b7f-8a58-11a84470416e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376144 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-4,1)$ and passes through the point $(0,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-4,1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-1)^{2}=4p(x+4).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,3),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-1)^{2} & =4p(0+4) \\\\ 4 & =4p(4) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-1)^{2} & =x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-1)^{2} & =x+4 \\\\ 1 & =x+4 \\\\ 1-4 & =x \\\\ x & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-3.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376146 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376147 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376148 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376149 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376150 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376145 1