a5db86-222d-5daf-a37d-67620070082e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376496 1081 "6\\,∣\\,18({4}^{2k+1})" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376496 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376496 1084 #uuid "ed6fe9d6-bba2-5169-8e1e-f9db1fd7b6fb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376498 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376503 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376508 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1069 "q-183625" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1071 "Given that $|R\\times R|=c,$ complete the following reasoning about the cardinality of the set $R\\times [-5,6):$\n\nSince the function $f:(x,y)\\to (x,y)$ (that maps any ordered pair to itself) is an injection from $R\\times [-5,6)$ into $R\\times R,$ and \n\n$$\ng:(x,y)\\to (x,{{field-1}}{{field-2}})\n$$\n\nis an injection from $R\\times R$ onto $R\\times (-5,5)⊆R\\times [-5,6),$ according to Cantor-Bernstein-Schröder theorem, we have that \n$|R\\times [-5,6)|=$ {{field-3}}." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1072 #uuid "e59adc9d-1486-5639-aee0-0f6f33d30bc8" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376497 1074 "According to the Cantor-Bernstein-Schröder theorem, if $|A|\\le |B|$ and $|B|\\le |A|,$ then $|A|=|B|.$ \n\nIn other words, if there exist injections $f:A\\to B$ and $g:B\\to A,$ then there exists a bijection between $A$ and $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, we note the following:\n\n- The function $f:(x,y)\\to (x,y)$ (that maps any ordered pair to itself) is an injection from $R\\times [-5,6)$ into $R\\times R.$ So, we have \n\n$$\n|R\\times [-5,6)|\\le |R\\times R|.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the function\n\n$$\nx\\to x\n$$\n\ninjectively maps $R\\to R,$ and \n\n$$\ny\\to \\frac{10}{\\pi }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y)\n$$\n\ninjectively maps $R$ onto $(-5,5)⊆[-5,6).$ Thus,\n\n$$\ng:(x,y)\\to (x,\\frac{10}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y))\n$$\n\nis an injection from $R\\times R$ onto $R\\times (-5,5)⊆R\\times [-5,6),$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/af/af4472ba9056eaf9c62c7dca99de4904339aff6dbf0de8d1225bc41b0fde9c00.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n|R\\times R|\\le |R\\times [-5,6)|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Cantor-Bernstein-Schröder theorem, \n\n$$\n|R\\times [-5,6)|=|R\\times R|=c.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376501 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376502 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1079 #edb/ref 17592186376502 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376498 1080 #uuid "9754a5c9-22e3-53ff-b7a1-de2028f9f8cd" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376499 1081 "\\frac{5}{\\pi }" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376499 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376499 1084 #uuid "d4b7733a-d12d-5486-9954-151fe94f6cd1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376500 1081 "\\frac{10}{7}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376500 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376500 1084 #uuid "c04a3865-ba20-52eb-9f69-439e058f6f05" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376501 1081 "\\frac{5}{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376501 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376501 1084 #uuid "3fa43bf2-3c36-5fc6-9303-d0653fb81171" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376502 1081 "\\frac{10}{\\pi }" 1319413953345