585 true] [17592186376513 1072 #uuid "e6e56f8d-6c40-5576-a57d-3ec0aca57256" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376513 1074 "Let's denote:\n\n- $P(n):\\,\\sqrt{n}\\notin N$\n\n- $Q(n):\\,n∣2$\n\nThen, our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∃n\\,P(n)⇒∀n\\,Q(n).\n$$\n\nBy eliminating implication, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∃n\\,P(n)⇒∀n\\,Q(n) & ≡¬(∃n\\,P(n))∨∀n\\,Q(n) \\\\  & ≡∀n\\,¬P(n)∨∀n\\,Q(n)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't \"factor out\" the quantifier since, in general, \n\n$$\n∀n\\,P(n)∨∀n\\,Q(n)≢∀n\\,(P(n)∨Q(n)).\n$$\n\nHowever, we can change the variable in one of the predicates. For example, in the second one:\n\n$$\n∀n\\,P(n)∨∀n\\,Q(n)≡∀n\\,P(n)∨∀m\\,Q(m)\n$$\n\nNow, since $P(n)$ does not depend on $m$ and $Q(m)$ does not depend on $n,$ we can move the quantifiers to the front, as follows:\n\n$$\n∀n\\,¬P(n)∨∀m\\,Q(m)≡∀n\\,∀m\\,(¬P(n)∨Q(m))\n$$\n\nThe final expression reads \n\n$\\,$ $∀n,m\\in N\\,(\\sqrt{n}\\in N∨m∣2).$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376515 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376516 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376517 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376518 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376519 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1079 #edb/ref 17592186376517 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376514 1080 #uuid "9f70b996-83eb-5d06-8f36-764b5086d564" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376515 1081 "∀n\\in N\\,(\\sqrt{n}\\notin N∨n∣2)" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376515 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186376515 1084 #uuid "fe0da3f7-17d2-586c-8491-94433a05889b" 13194139533452 17592186045