re\n\n$$\nx=(-\\frac{1}{2}){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-\\frac{1}{2})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,y=-t.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377042 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377043 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377042 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377042 1077 "field-2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377042 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377043 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377042 1080 #uuid "2f4974bc-e074-545a-be7a-908a290a5eed" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377043 1081 "-t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377043 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377043 1084 #uuid "d89a6c8c-1c3d-5e8e-8f2a-b1ac6ad21803" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377044 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377045 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377044 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377044 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377044 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377045 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377044 1080 #uuid "22765ed4-0cc6-5277-848a-48261dabb73f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377045 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377045 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377045 1084 #uuid "a12c9776-03d6-5a18-9c43-cdc37ebe7a8b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377047 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1069 "q-276278" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2t+5,\\,\\,\\,y=(t-2)(t+1),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1072 #uuid "22eb775d-0ea8-57a9-a014-0d8618741de6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377046 1074 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2t+5\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{x-5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{x-5}{2}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(\\frac{x-5}{2}-2)(\\frac{x-5}{2}+1) \\\\  & =(\\frac{x-5-4}{2})(\\frac{x-5+2}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{x-9}{2})(\\frac{x-3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(x-9)(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377047 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377048 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377047 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377047 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377047 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377048 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377047 1080 #uuid "e36531d7-495c-5197-b612-e0e22cd3b3b5" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377048 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}(x-9)(x-3)" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377048 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377048 1084 #uuid "33526b37-cab0-5457-9e07-446f0c05aa08" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377050 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377052 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1069 "q-280198" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1071 "![](images/23/23fa9b0f268e953cf9a2b770c3a3cb83c64fa0217a55e3a5313c81bf6933fc0a.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the above parabola. Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1072 #uuid "659b155d-7a86-5ce4-a60f-a888671f046c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377049 1074 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(1,2).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(1,2),$ we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=2$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}1=2pt \\\\ 2=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =2pt \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{2p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =p{(\\frac{1}{2p})}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{4{p}^{2}} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{1}{4p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(\\frac{1}{8})t,\\,y=(\\frac{1}{8}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{4}t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377050 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377051 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377050 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377050 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377050 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377051 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377050 1080 #uuid "8ad9a621-dd17-56d4-9033-7136556fc8ea" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377051 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377051 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377051 1084 #uuid "b8e2d09a-689d-5e58-a00e-c11460b13e09" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377052 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377053 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377052 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [175921