olving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =p{(\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -1 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{4}{p} \\\\ p & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(-4)t,\\,y=(-4){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-8t,\\,y=-4{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377055 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377056 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377055 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377055 1077 "field-2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377055 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377056 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377055 1080 #uuid "81a105c3-b080-5c79-b83a-4614140f393e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377056 1081 "-4{t}^{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377056 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377056 1084 #uuid "37408f16-b913-5fff-9939-14af701125d9" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377058 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377057 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377057 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377057 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377058 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377057 1080 #uuid "0129630e-e038-5d41-a51e-42a6c95e0206" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377058 1081 "-8t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377058 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377058 1084 #uuid "7f907296-0315-56bf-93ac-6dd5b6b8873c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377060 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377062 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1069 "q-280221" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1071 "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate a vertical parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and which passes through the point $(-2,4).$ Express your answer in the form $x=2pt,y=p{t}^{2},$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1072 #uuid "b87ecaed-5da1-505a-bfd4-108852c3407b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377059 1074 "The parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-2,4),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2=2pt \\\\ 4=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{1}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =p{(-\\frac{1}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 4 & =p\\cdot \\frac{1}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{1}{p} \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(\\frac{1}{4})t,\\,y=(\\frac{1}{4}){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377060 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377061 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377060 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377060 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377060 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377061 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377060 1080 #uuid "ba131a57-7ffc-54c1-b039-86518a03e7c3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377061 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}t" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377061 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 tru