#edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377088 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+4,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n{{field-1}}$=1.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377088 1072 #uuid "1c9558ce-37ee-554b-ae06-97c014ed01c5" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377088 1074 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+4\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=y-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2}+{(\\frac{x}{2})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+(y-4)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377089 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377090 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377089 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377089 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377089 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377090 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377089 1080 #uuid "505822d3-763e-5bdd-b961-64b75dcd3eb1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377090 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+(y-4)^{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377090 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377090 1084 #uuid "444c47c5-f6ff-5993-9810-f2a59d46e7f1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377092 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1069 "q-320878" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3t-1,\\,\\,\\,y=(t+5)(t-2),\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1072 #uuid "081bb8fa-7465-5289-83b2-398e18ea3051" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377091 1074 "To find the Cartesian equation, we eliminate $t.$ First, we use the $x$ equation to solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=3t-1\\,⇒\\,t=\\frac{x+1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $t=\\frac{x+1}{3}$ into our expression for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =(\\frac{x+1}{3}+5)(\\frac{x+1}{3}-2) \\\\  & =(\\frac{x+1+15}{3})(\\frac{x+1-6}{3}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{x+16}{3})(\\frac{x-5}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(x+16)(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377092 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377093 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377092 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377092 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377092 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377093 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377092 1080 #uuid "d4e1d208-e4d2-5915-83c1-b4b15806c88a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377093 1081 "\\frac{1}{9}(x+16)(x-5)" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377093 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377093 1084 #uuid "e76ec15d-4235-56b9-b033-fb60f2aa5631" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377095 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1069 "q-321315" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t,\\,t\\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nThe Cartesian equation of this curve is\n\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1072 #uuid "e0deecc2-15f7-5c26-991c-e45282132b63" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377094 1074 "First, let's make the trigonometric functions the subject of each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{4} \\\\ y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\, & ⇒\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the double-angle formula for cosine and the Pythagorean identity, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & ={cos}^{2}⁡t-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡t) \\\\  & =2{cos}^{2}⁡t-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t=-\\frac{x}{4}$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t=\\frac{y}{3}$ into this formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{3} & =2{(-\\frac{x}{4})}^{2}-1 \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-1 \\\\ y & =3(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-1) \\\\ y & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the given curve is $y=\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}-3.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377095 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377096 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377095 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377095 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377095 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377096 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377095 1080 #uuid "3733f8ba-81a2-59af-8065-3da7adf791ea" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377096 1081 "\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8}-3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377096 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377096 1084 #uuid "dfd39e46-6e10-5277-9820-57dd084b55b4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377097 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377098 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377097 1069 "q-321400" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377097 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377097 1071 "Consider the curve defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\,\\,y=2\\operatorname{csc}⁡t,\\,0<t<\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe Carte