 LU decomposition $A=LU$, then ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377113 1072 #uuid "e406fe00-7a29-5a99-8344-99701140afc2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377113 1074 "To find the matrices $L$ and $U,$ we reduce the matrix $A$ to row echelon form. Whilst doing this, we simultaneously write down the row operations applied to $A$ in terms of matrix multiplication using elementary matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{1}\\,⟺\\,\\overset{{E}_{1}}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot A \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix is upper triangular, so it is our matrix $U.$ Now, since ${E}_{1}A=U,$ we can invert ${E}_{1}$ to arrive at the desired LU factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}_{1}A & =U \\\\ A & ={E}_{1}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}U \\\\ A & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{L}{{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{U}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${l}_{21}=-1,{u}_{22}=0,$ and ${l}_{21}+{u}_{22}=-1.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377115 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377116 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377117 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377118 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377119 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377119 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377114 1080 #uuid "7845731f-9fba-5548-afdf-a930581719a8" 13194139533452 17592186045