3194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377143 1072 #uuid "af59844e-c235-5324-b1ce-bf9372a53e14" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377143 1074 "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nThe forcing term\n\n$$\n{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nof the inhomogeneous system of ODEs is exponential. Therefore, we assume that the particular solution is also exponential, i.e.\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)={e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere $a,b$  are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the derivative of ${x}_{p}$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}^{′}(t)=-5{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the unknown constants, we substitute ${x}_{p}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}$ into our system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{-5t}[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ -5[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5a \\\\ -5b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2a+b \\\\ 2b\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}-5a \\\\ -5b\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2a+b+8 \\\\ 2b+7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2a+b+8=-5a \\\\ 2b+7=-5b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n2b+7=-5b\\,⇒\\,b=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $a,$ we have\n\n$$\n2a+(-1)+8=-5a\\,⇒\\,a=-1.\