^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{4}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-x){|}_{-1}^{1}\\,+\\,(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}-1-(\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}-(-1))]\\,+\\,[4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}-1-(-\\frac{1}{3}+1)]\\,+\\,12 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}+12 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377367 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377368 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377367 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377367 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377367 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377368 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377367 1080 #uuid "69592282-c254-5033-b9af-1fa76ca679ea" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377368 1081 "\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377368 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377368 1084 #uuid "fcdc16d7-c730-5e33-ba9c-dc66b5b6c13f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377370 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1069 "q-343470" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1071 "![](images/b5/b5f89f7cab8f4dde051c7a5e11cdd64d9de7c5c681d842d33a957387adbd6ab7.png)\n\nConsider the graph of the function $f(x),$ shown above. It consists of three line segments. Find the value of\n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1072 #uuid "bdcffa54-7028-56e4-abd2-481f88c69b76" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377369 1074 "The graph consists of $3$ parts: the line segment for $x\\in [-3,0],$ the line segment for $x\\in [0,2],$ and the line segment for $x\\in [2,4].$ Therefore, we can write the 