e curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [-1,1].$ The corresponding region is a combination of a semi-circle and a square, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2}+{a}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {1}^{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe $3$rd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [1,3].$ The corresponding region is a quarter-circle centred at $(1,0),$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2}+{A}_{3} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{2}+4+\\pi  \\\\  & =4+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377385 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377386 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377385 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377385 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377385 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377386 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377385 1080 #uuid "9bac7d03-0106-5250-9c6a-307d4ff537f9" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377386 1081 "4+\\frac{5\\pi }{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377386 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377386 1084 #uuid "6c49f045-2e2a-5dd8-9bbc-8ddd139c4b6b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377387 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377388 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377387 1069 "q-344476" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377387 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377387 1071 "![](images/5e/5e73df02e9a1fc485decba51c44befd02a220898d93891511ce96e6eb33d1835.png)\n\nConsider the graph of the function $f(x),$ shown above. It consists of two line segments