}$ be the rate at which the amount of charge stored is changing and let $A(T)$ be the amount of charge stored $T$ seconds after charging begins. \n\nUsing our formula for the accumulation of change, we have\n\n$$\nA(T)=A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known information and carrying out the necessary integration gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(T) & =A(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{T}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7+{\\int }_{0}^{T}\\frac{40}{(t+1)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =7+(-\\frac{20}{(t+1)^{2}}){|}_{0}^{T} \\\\  & =7+(-\\frac{20}{(T+1)^{2}})-(-\\frac{20}{{1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =7-\\frac{20}{(T+1)^{2}}+20 \\\\  & =27-\\frac{20}{(T+1)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount of charge stored $T=1$ second after charging begins, we substitute in the above:\n\n$$\nA(1)=7-\\frac{20}{(1+1)^{2}}+20=22.\n$$\n\nThus, after $1$ second, the device stores $22$ coulombs of charge." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377540 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377539 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377539 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377539 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377540 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377539 1080 #uuid "84701d8c-3c1c-5940-b9a1-9b8b85613cc8" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377540 1081 "22" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377540 1084 #uuid "dadac5c6-a33d-5ec0-8085-af08c5a4bf3c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377542 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1069 "q-350536" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{10{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{5}+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1072 #uuid "3bc676ae-5eea-5c37-8152-babd81d7b946" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377541 1074 "First, we substitute $u={x}^{5}+1.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5{x}^{4}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=5{x}^{4}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{5}+1$ is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\infty $ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\infty $ |\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{10{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{5}+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{u}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}u\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\frac{10{x}^{4}}{\\sqrt{({x}^{5}+1)^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{u}^{9}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }2{u}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}2{u}^{-9/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[-\\frac{4}{7}{u}^{-7/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[{u}^{-7/2}]}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\frac{1}{{a}^{7/2}}-\\frac{1}{{1}^{7/2}}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{7}\\cdot (0-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377542 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377543 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377542 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377542 1077 "field-1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377542 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377543 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377542 1080 #uuid "482395fb-c7fb-5370-bf50-f7fa1aec416c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377543 1081 "\\frac{4}{7}" 13194139533452 175921