x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =12+2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377576 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377577 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377578 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377579 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377580 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377577 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377575 1080 #uuid "59c92177-9ded-5c63-9cb3-4c4f4a2d25b9" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377576 1081 "6+4\\pi " 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377576 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377576 1084 #uuid "a0548f28-a84c-5788-9dd5-1ea59549840c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377577 1081 "12+2\\pi " 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377577 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377577 1084 #uuid "807dad30-2355-54f9-8046-27068d7ea408" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377578 1081 "12+4\\pi " 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377578 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377578 1084 #uuid "f8ec02d2-f9a0-5fad-ba9d-4e446fcc9661" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377579 1081 "6+2\\pi " 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377579 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377579 1084 #uuid "12ea0440-97a1-5184-9d99-be591e1d199a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377580 1081 "12+3\\pi " 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377580 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377580 1084 #uuid "0a2f2dcd-e4d2-5a84-bc71-1dbf0587c8ce" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377582 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1069 "q-36067" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1071 "Consider the lines $3y-kx=3$ and $x+2y=0$, where $k$ is a constant. If both intersect at one point, then" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1072 #uuid "8426bbc0-cdc8-595a-941b-da128b255dca" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377581 1074 "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\nAccording to the invertible matrix theorem, if the lines $-kx+3y=3$ and $x+2y=0$ intersect at one point, then\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-k & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis invertible and $det(A)\\ne 0$, which implies that ${A}^{-1}$ exists ($A$ is non-singular). Additionally, the unique solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=⟨0,0⟩$ and\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-k & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nhas exactly one solution, which is the intersection point of the lines." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377582 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377583 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377582 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377584 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377582 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377585 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [1