 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377599 1084 #uuid "6a4907ea-6955-5231-bd49-965eb90809fb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377601 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1069 "q-49812" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1071 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1072 #uuid "028b6dfa-ac89-5974-9044-6dccd3022ba4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377600 1074 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)-x+D) \\\\  & =x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+2x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={(x{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+2x)|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =(e{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2e\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)+2e)-(1{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+2(1)) \\\\  & =e-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377602 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377603 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377604 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377605 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377606 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377602 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377601 1080 #uuid "f324bdac-71ef-525e-9a4a-7e229f1a660d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377602 1081 "e-2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377602 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377602 1084 #uuid "595c803c-cc37-5acf-8d28-de44643dd96f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186