585 true] [17592186377647 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377647 1071 "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=1$, in ascending powers of $(x-1)$ up to and including the term in $(x-1)^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=y\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+2{y}^{′},\\,y(1)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=1.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377647 1072 #uuid "d87aabd3-74be-52a2-9016-f7c8a3c0130b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377647 1074 "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=1$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(1)$ and ${y}^{′}(1),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{″}(1)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(1).$\n\nWe substitute $y(1)=4$ and ${y}^{′}(1)=1$ into the given equation to find ${y}^{″}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(1) & =y(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2{y}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)={y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{y}{x}+2{y}^{″}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(1)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(1) & ={y}^{′}(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{y(1)}{1}+2{y}^{″}(1) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+4+2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinaly, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(1)+(x-1){y}^{′}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(1)+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(1)+⋯ \\\\  & =4+(x-1)\\cdot 1+\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}\\cdot 2+\\frac{(x-1)^{3}}{6}\\cdot 8+… \\\\  & =4+(x-1)+(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}(x-1)^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377649 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377650 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377651 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377652 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377653 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377653 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377648 1080 #uuid "7b56f06b-2202-59a5-80b5-a40aacc9c336" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377649 1081 "y(x)=4+(x-1)+(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{3}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377649 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377649 1084 #uuid "e86cbbc6-df7a-5a1d-a605-be1de296c3e8" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377650 1081 "y(x)=4+(x-1)+(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377650 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377650 1084 #uuid "21fc0fb5-2e7c-5603-8a94-cdc54d061d18" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377651 1081 "y(x)=4+(x-1)+2(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377651 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377651 1084 #uuid "1b3879a4-02c0-5761-80f7-474cff02f490" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377652 1081 "y(x)=4+(x-1)+2(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{6}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377652 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377652 1084 #uuid "dd4dd95f-d5a5-5afb-b79d-5e7968ce30d0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377653 1081 "y(x)=4+(x-1)+(x-1)^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}(x-1)^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377653 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377653 1084 #uuid "e9f8a93c-905b-531c-910f-4941b4fe3b9d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377655 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1069 "q-64999" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1071 "![](images/7f/7ffcda47f0d750ce9f25e50b0b28091ff4279467313fbe604eac0fc9b1229806.png)\n\nConsider the set $M,$ depicted by the shaded region above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is an interior point of the set $M$\n- $B$ is a boundary point of the set $M$\n- $C$ is a boundary point of the set $M$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1072 #uuid "10cee0d6-c023-521a-a779-cab7a62d3b8f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377654 1074 "Let $\\delta >0.$ A *neighborhood* of a point ${x}_{0}$ is the set of points whose distance from ${x}_{0}$ is less than $\\delta .$\n\n$$\n{x:|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta }\n$$\n\nIn two-dimensional space, a neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ is the open disc $|x-{x}_{0}|<\\delta ,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/50/50a6c72e169f3104eb0b9958673cc6644f770e6bcc3ebf23360eb20189325a28.png)\n\nFurthermore, we have the following definitions:\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is an *interior point* of a set $S$ if $S$ contains *some* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}.$ The set of all interior points of $S$ is called the *interior* of $S.$\n\n- A point ${x}_{0}$ is a *boundary point* of a set $S$ if *every* neighborhood of ${x}_{0}$ contains points that are in $S$ and points that are not in $S.$ \nThe set of all boundary points of $S$ is called the *boundary* of $S.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](images/08/080d6cf1cd468b7ddfe65df2e6a21792e1afe470ddd571c6b5ec25569d1fb537.png)\n\n- Statement I is false. Every open neighborhood of $A$ contains points that belong to \n$M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$ The point $A$ is a boundary point for the given set.\n\n- Statement II is true. The point $B$ is a boundary point because every open neighborhood of $B$ contains points that belong to $M$ and points that do not belong to $M.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, $C$ is an interior point since there exists an open neighborhood of $C$ that is fully contained inside the set $M.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 'II only'." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377656 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377657 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377658 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377659 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377660 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377660 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377655 1080 #uuid "01a35593-4c9e-5037-b87f-d4e48a3bf713" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377656 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377656 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377656 1084 #uuid "696e584f-f454-593e-bd58-abb69e57b3af" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377657 1081 "I only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377657 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377657 1084 #uuid "a3452674-e7ae-5e7f-858b-9637d1e75a98" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377658 1081 "III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377658 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377658 1084 #uuid "a978c7d2-6987-586e-9304-4ae71f2c36a9" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377659 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377659 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377659 1084 #uuid "e1c