2186377733 1084 #uuid "a538c059-9365-52d6-b129-5e6c9890bfb6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377735 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1069 "q-77650" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1071 "Find a Cartesian equation of the osculating plane for the curve $r(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, given that\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,-{t}^{2}⟩,\\,T(0)=⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩,\\,N(0)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\n$$\n\nwhere $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1072 #uuid "54c36bce-c36b-52fd-b9ca-a0e6051f8c36" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377734 1074 "The position vector of the point where $t=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p=r(0) & =⟨-2(0),\\,{0}^{2},\\,{0}^{2}⟩=⟨0,\\,0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find a vector that's perpendicular to the osculating plane. To do that, we use the cross product of the unit tangent $T(0)$ and the principal normal $N(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0)\\times N(0) & =⟨-1,\\,0,\\,0⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we are interested only in the direction of the above vector, let's write our perpendicular vector $n$ as \n\n$$\nn=-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (T(0)\\times N(0))=⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, let $⟨x,y,z⟩$ denote the position vector of a point on the osculating plane. Since the plane is perpendicular to $n$ and passes through the tip of the position vector $p$, its Cartesian equation can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(⟨x,y,z⟩-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ & =⟨0,0,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ 0\\cdot x+1\\cdot y+1\\cdot z & =0 \\\\ y+z & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377736 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377737 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377738 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377739 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377740 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377740 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377735 1080 #uuid "e11d19ec-ccc1-5cd9-af43-437bf54e3751" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377736 1081 "x+y+z=0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377736 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377736 1084 #uuid "82538c6f-88d8-500c-88b1-74eb634f6a90" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377737 1081 "z=0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377737 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377737 1084 #uuid "e43479cf-b8c9-5835-9dff-896a2ed0ce2c" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377738 1081 "x+z=0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377738 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377738 1084 #uuid "495a2db5-a585-5c5c-91d8-2b8c96fc9f85" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377739 1081 "x+y=0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377739 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377739 1084 #uuid "8ed7424e-fab7-5e6a-97e6-0d07d8032d0f" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377740 1081 "y+z=0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377740 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377740 1084 #uuid "3309df00-5376-5ed7-97ab-65a3a552c687" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377742 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1069 "q-78576" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1071 "If $U=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]$, then ${U}^{3}=$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1072 #uuid "07ba9ea7-a44e-52e4-bff2-32246bba4f40" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377741 1074 "First, we compute ${U}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${U}^{2}=U,$ so $U$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${U}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & ={U}^{2} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{U}^{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377743 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377744 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377745 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377746 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377742 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377747 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [175921863