rue] [17592186377755 1072 #uuid "73f63cef-323f-560b-95b0-2cf7424d4b67" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377755 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-4,-4)$ and passes through the point $(2,14).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(-4,-4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x+4)^{2}=4p(y+4).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(2,14),$ we substitute $x=2$ and $y=14$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+4)^{2} & =4p(14+4) \\\\ 36 & =4p(18) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+4)^{2} & =2(y+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+4)^{2} & =2(y+4) \\\\ 16 & =2(y+4) \\\\ 8 & =y+4 \\\\ y & =8-4 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $4.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377757 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377758 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377759 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377760 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377761 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377760 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377756 1080 #uuid "14445e32-9654-51bf-beee-75e82df1a60a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377757 1081 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377757 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377757 1084 #uuid "adb19221-6751-5cef-8343-237e49f76b8e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377758 1081 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377758 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377758 1084 #uuid "cf2ff7e8-ce07-586f-ba77-b3cdd3b65295" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377759 1081 "6" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377759 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377759 1084 #uuid "042523a7-042d-5186-805a-f9d126ddff27" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377760 1081 "4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377760 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377760 1084 #uuid "fd12f48e-79a8-5156-a46c-4b1e32cf7d5b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377761 1081 "5" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377761 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377761 1084 #uuid "2189c154-a254-5c78-a00c-3410a2a2fc64" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377763 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1069 "q-79352" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1071 "Find $\\text{rank}(A)$ given that $\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1072 #uuid "0131f756-450c-5ffd-bd43-d0c24b54342a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377762 1074 "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4,$ since this is the number of components in each of the vectors of the null space. \n\nAlso, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}\\in R}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that $\\text{nullity}(A)=3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+3 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377764 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377765 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377766 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377767 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377768 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377766 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377763 1080 #uuid "0ef6c019-6203-53f2-a536-cc2b8d76a9fb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377764 1081 "3" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377764 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377764 1084 #uuid "aca86402-c665-55ad-96e2-e7faee870cc9" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377765 1081 "2" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377765 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377765 1084 #uuid "701ec281-64bf-55a9-a13a-9af209eaff5e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377766 1081 "1" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377766 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377766 1084 #uuid "93249bda-5da5-5cfd-8d15-56c91976394d" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377767 1081 "4" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377767 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377767 1084 #uuid "60b2f467-bf50-5ae6-993c-21e4a93659ef" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377768 1081 "0" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377768 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377768 1084 #uuid "cfdd441a-d8f0-5c12-b7bc-0bc161b02d98" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377770 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1069 "q-79367" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1071 "Which of the following statements are true given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix with $3$ pivot columns?\n\n- $\\text{rank}(A)=3$\n- $A$ is not  invertible\n- $\\text{nullity}(A)=3$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1072 #uuid "2c7ff497-8845-5d34-a5a1-e0b10d7a1e25" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377769 1074 "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{5} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=5=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nAlso, according to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since $A$ has $3$ pivot columns, we have $\\text{rank}(A)=3.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for the matrix $A,$ the number of the columns is $n=5.$ Now, since $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5,$ then by the invertible matrix theorem,  $A$ can't be an invertible matrix.\n\n- Statement III is false. According to  the rank-nullity theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 3+\\text{nullity}(A) & =5 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =5-3 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377771 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377772 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377773 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377774 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377775 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377775 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377770 1080 #uuid "9ef75295-8f00-53ba-bcd0-1da090f1e272" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377771 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377771 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377771 1084 #uuid "6a7cc05b-4143-5191-a5e9-d4ab94e09a0b" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377772 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377772 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377772 1084 #uuid "d0184665-f93e-563e-82f8-842a76f9bd8a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377773 1081 "I only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377773 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377773 1084 #uuid "590f4fb6-6508-551b-9c11-b1551e26a497" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377774 1081 "III only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377774 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377774 1084 #uuid "ff9bc119-5748-526f-9158-ef10267d3396" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377775 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377775 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377775 1084 #uuid "8bd0dd26-4f04-5458-99f5-876504ceec53" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1068 #edb/ref 17592186377777 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1069 "q-79952" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1071 "Use the Taylor series method to find a series solution about $x=0$, in ascending powers of $x$ up to and including the term in ${x}^{3},$  of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}={y}^{2}-2{e}^{x},\\,y(0)=0.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1072 #uuid "13e60b71-ea19-538e-b326-669602e65dde" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377776 1074 "We wish to express $y(x)$ as a Taylor series about $x=0$:\n\n$$\ny(x)=y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯\n$$\n\nWe're given $y(0),$ so we need to calculate ${y}^{′}(0),$  ${y}^{″}(0)$ and ${y}^{(3)}(0).$\n\nWe know that $y(0)=0,$ so we substitute this into the given equation to find ${y}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & ={y}^{2}(0)-2{e}^{0}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find an expression for ${y}^{″}(x),$ we differentiate both sides on the given equation with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)=2y{y}^{′}-2{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{″}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{″}(0) & =2y(0){y}^{′}(0)-2{e}^{0} \\\\  & =2(0)(-2)-2 \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find an expression for ${y}^{(3)}(x),$ we differentiate ${y}^{″}(x)$ with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n{y}^{(3)}(x)=2{y}^{′}{y}^{′}+2y{y}^{″}-2{e}^{x}=2({y}^{′})^{2}+2y{y}^{″}-2{e}^{x}\n$$\n\nWe can now find  ${y}^{(3)}(0)$ by substituting in the known values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{(3)}(0) & =2({y}^{′}(0))^{2}+2y(0){y}^{″}(0)-2{e}^{0} \\\\  & =2(-2)^{2}+2(0)(-2)-2{e}^{0} \\\\  & =8+0-2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we  substitute  the obtained values in  the Taylor series:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =y(0)+x{y}^{′}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}{y}^{″}(0)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}{y}^{(3)}(0)+⋯ \\\\  & =0+x\\cdot (-2)+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\cdot (-2)+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}\\cdot 6+⋯ \\\\  & =-2x-{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377778 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377779 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377780 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377781 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377782 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377779 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377777 1080 #uuid "94a985d8-998d-51e5-a4f6-2ab89021f4bd" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377778 1081 "y=-2x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{3}{x}^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377778 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377778 1084 #uuid "ab36413d-f943-5fe3-a60d-a7a536d4869a" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377779 1081 "y=-2x-{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377779 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377779 1084 #uuid "091b84bd-5d67-5c30-9f5e-75dd64dc99fb" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377780 1081 "y=2x+{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+⋯" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377780 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377780 1084 #uuid "00b1537c-b979-56ea-98e0-9f713104cf48" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377781 1081 "y=2x-{x}^{2}+\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{3}+⋯" 13194139