y\n\n$$\n{e}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{e}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe components of the vectors in $B$ are just the coordinates relative to the standard basis:\n\n$$\n[{b}_{1}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{2}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],\\,[{b}_{3}]_{S}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $B$ relative to the basis $S.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=0,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-5.$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377852 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377853 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377854 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377855 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377856 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377852 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377851 1080 #uuid "e78e9f40-0718-5bad-956f-0b197faf152e" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377852 1081 "$a=0,$ $b=-1,$ and $c=-5$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377852 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377852 1084 #uuid "c4d259b5-915f-51f3-b82a-a4a9da133e01" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377853 1081 "$a=3,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377853 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533452 