 need to find the coordinates of ${e}_{1}$ and ${e}_{2}$ relative to the basis $B.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & {e}_{1} & {e}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we simply reduce the left-hand side to reduced row-echelon form using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 11 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the right-hand side, we obtain the change-of-coordinates matrix from $S$ to $B.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{P}_{S\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377859 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377860 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377861 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377862 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377863 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377862 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377858 1080 #uuid "ab9e6ef9-e9ea-5c1f-ad73-6228ba8a6770" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377859 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}6 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377859 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377859 1084 #uuid "070ecd32-2b28-56a5-85bd-6a34995dde85" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377860 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}25 & -5 \\\\ -