ab01c602db67da1291dc9.png)\n\nWhich of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the parabola shown above?" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377906 1072 #uuid "8bf28229-05a6-5b2e-8652-9947e15e4e53" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377906 1074 "The diagram shows that the parabola is vertical, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(6,3).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a vertical parabola  that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=2pt,\\,y=p{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(6,3),$ we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=3$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}6=2pt \\\\ 3=p{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving the first equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =2pt \\\\ 3 & =pt \\\\ t & =\\frac{3}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =p{(\\frac{3}{p})}^{2} \\\\ 3 & =p\\cdot \\frac{9}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{9}{p} \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=2(3)t,\\,y=(3){t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=6t,\\,y=3{t}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377908 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377909 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377910 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377911 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1075 #edb/ref 17592186377912 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1077 "selection" 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1079 #edb/ref 17592186377909 13194139533452 17592186045585 true] [17592186377907 1080 #u